From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@local>
Date: Mon, 18 May 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] streambox-tv: enable low-latency HDMI setup in headless

When HDMI TX is disconnected, streambox-tv enters headless capture-only
mode and skips the whole STREAM_BOX low-latency initialization block.
On VIM4 this leaves HDMI RX/VDIN unstable: /dev/video_cap opens, but no
frames are produced.

Run the same ALLM/VRR/game-mode setup in headless mode before StartTv()
so capture-only operation follows the working hdmiin-demo path.
---
 test/streambox-tv.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/test/streambox-tv.c b/test/streambox-tv.c
--- a/test/streambox-tv.c
+++ b/test/streambox-tv.c
@@ -1987,7 +1987,7 @@
          __FUNCTION__, video->game_mode, video->vrr_mode, video->hdmi_source);
 
 #ifdef STREAM_BOX
-    if (video->game_mode > 0 && !g_headless_mode) {
+    if (video->game_mode > 0) {
         int ret;
 
         /* Enable ALLM (Auto Low Latency Mode) - always enabled */
@@ -2011,7 +2011,7 @@
         int game_mode_value = (video->game_mode == 2) ? 3 : 1;
         ret = SetGameMode(pTvClientWrapper, 1, game_mode_value);
         if (ret == 0) {
-            LOGD("Game Mode enabled successfully (game_mode_value=%d)\n", game_mode_value);
+            LOGD("Game Mode enabled successfully (game_mode_value=%d, headless=%d)\n", game_mode_value, g_headless_mode);
         } else {
             LOGD("Failed to enable Game Mode, ret=%d\n", ret);
         }
